        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Notes are plain JSON on disk, one file per note:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeBlock",
      "attrs": {
        "language": "text"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "~/Documents/Novion/\n├── workspace.json   the tree\n├── docs/            one JSON file per note\n├── assets/          images\n└── history/         version snapshots"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Backing up means copying the folder. Under Settings → Storage you can move the whole workspace to iCloud Drive and share it between Macs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "bookmark",
      "attrs": {
        "url": "https://www.notion.so",
        "title": "Notion two-way sync",
        "description": "Push local edits to Notion, and pull Notion edits back."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Settings → Notion mirrors the workspace to a Notion page: folders become subpages, notes become pages. Edits travel in both directions, and conflicts are never overwritten — you are asked case by case."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
